# Solidity sources are checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# solc hashes the source bytes into the metadata it appends to the bytecode, so
# the same contract compiled from a CRLF checkout and an LF one produces the
# same code with a different trailing metadata hash. That broke the one promise
# lib/verify/sim-artifact.ts makes, which is that `npm run build:verify-sim`
# reproduces it byte for byte: on Windows, with core.autocrlf on, it could not.
# The committed artifact is built from LF, so the working tree has to be LF too.
*.sol text eol=lf

# The generated artifact itself, for the same reason: it is compared byte for
# byte against a fresh build in CI.
lib/verify/sim-artifact.ts text eol=lf
